# C9D Identity — @c9d/auth-next (Next.js server SDK)

## Use

Use `@c9d/auth-next` when implementing server-side auth flow plumbing in product Next.js apps:

- middleware/proxy unauthenticated redirects
- route handlers for `/auth/login`, `/auth/callback`, `/auth/logout`
- server session retrieval (`getSession`)
- embedded bridge wrappers (`/api/auth/embedded/*`) using `createC9DEmbeddedBridge`

`@c9d/auth-next` composes framework-neutral primitives from `@c9d/auth-core`.

## Environment contract

Required:

- `C9D_IDENTITY_URL` (or `NEXT_PUBLIC_C9D_IDENTITY_URL`)
- `C9D_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID` (or `NEXT_PUBLIC_C9D_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID`)
- `C9D_SESSION_SECRET`

Optional confidential exchange:

- `C9D_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET` (server-only)

Never define `NEXT_PUBLIC_C9D_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET`.

## Security

- Token exchange and session signing stay server-side.
- Keep `C9D_SESSION_SECRET` and `C9D_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET` out of client bundles.
- OAuth redirect URIs must target the product callback (`/auth/callback`), not identity host callback.

